they're definitely not overpaid

01:10:24.480 --> 01:10:25.990
because they're paid based on the reality

01:10:25.990 --> 01:10:28.360
of what the market conditions created.

01:10:28.360 --> 01:10:31.200
We allowed them to be paid this way

01:10:31.200 --> 01:10:32.830
because we drive the revenue.

01:10:32.830 --> 01:10:35.490
If everybody wants to
stop watching football

01:10:35.490 --> 01:10:38.053
and drive that down, they're
more than welcome to.

01:10:39.270 --> 01:10:40.760
I've had a lot of fun
with a lot of my friends

01:10:40.760 --> 01:10:44.530
who take the other stance,
they don't like pro football.

01:10:44.530 --> 01:10:48.430
But when their homies at
Alabama, and LSU, and Texas

01:10:48.430 --> 01:10:50.800
start kneelin', they like their Longhorns.

01:10:50.800 --> 01:10:52.230
They care about their 'Bama boys.

01:10:52.230 --> 01:10:54.240
So it's been really interesting to watch.

01:10:54.240 --> 01:10:56.030
I have a lot of empathy

01:10:56.030 --> 01:10:57.850
and I'm super in tune with it

01:10:57.850 --> 01:10:59.995
because of the communist you know

01:10:59.995 --> 01:11:01.810
freedom of speech kind of thing.

01:11:01.810 --> 01:11:04.040
It's so deep in my, you
know, both my grandfathers

01:11:04.040 --> 01:11:07.930
spent ten years in jail in
Russia 'cause they were Jewish.

01:11:07.930 --> 01:11:11.510
So you know, I also have the benefit

01:11:11.510 --> 01:11:14.410
of having six of my eight
core friends in college

01:11:14.410 --> 01:11:18.070
be African-Americans which
led to me going to the mall

01:11:18.070 --> 01:11:19.390
the first four times in college

01:11:19.390 --> 01:11:21.330
and getting pulled over three times.

01:11:21.330 --> 01:11:23.140
Like the big thing that we're missing

01:11:23.140 --> 01:11:25.110
in our country right now is empathy.

01:11:25.110 --> 01:11:27.200
We're not putting ourselves
in other people's shoes,

01:11:27.200 --> 01:11:29.510
and we're letting
everything get politicized.

01:11:29.510 --> 01:11:31.450
Like are we gonna make
everything a political issue?

01:11:31.450 --> 01:11:35.560
Because basically we're in a
emotional civil war right now.

01:11:35.560 --> 01:11:36.790
Which is cool, I'm fine with it.

01:11:36.790 --> 01:11:38.403
Every empire should fall.

01:11:40.449 --> 01:11:41.282
- [Man In Blue Collared Shirt] Thank you.

01:11:41.282 --> 01:11:42.865
- You're welcome.

01:11:42.865 --> 01:11:44.236
- Andy, how are we on time?

01:11:44.236 --> 01:11:47.621
(audience applauding)

01:11:47.621 --> 01:11:48.454
- [Man In Gray shirt] Hey Gary.

01:11:48.454 --> 01:11:49.584
- Hey, brother.

01:11:49.584 --> 01:11:51.370
- You use a lot of fight analogies

01:11:51.370 --> 01:11:53.040
and we're in a room of
tons of martial artists

01:11:53.040 --> 01:11:54.061
and mixed martial artists.

01:11:54.061 --> 01:11:55.036
- [Gary] Yeah.

01:11:55.036 --> 01:11:57.043
- And I know VaynerSports

01:11:57.043 --> 01:11:59.690
I haven't seen any sign
in mixed martial artists.

01:11:59.690 --> 01:12:00.523
- [Gary] Nope.

01:12:00.523 --> 01:12:01.356
- I don't know if you guys

01:12:01.356 --> 01:12:03.331
with the UFC doing the
four billion dollar deal.

01:12:03.331 --> 01:12:04.530
- [Gary] Yup.

01:12:04.530 --> 01:12:08.490
- What do you think is the
future of mixed martial arts?

01:12:08.490 --> 01:12:11.460
What industry or opportunistically,

01:12:11.460 --> 01:12:12.293
what do you see coming for it?

01:12:12.293 --> 01:12:15.102
- Yeah, listen, fighting
is as old as ever.

01:12:15.102 --> 01:12:17.190
You know, it is core.

01:12:17.190 --> 01:12:20.305
It probably was the first sport, right?

01:12:20.305 --> 01:12:22.310
If I had to bet on it,
it was the first sport.

01:12:22.310 --> 01:12:23.940
Maybe racing you know,

01:12:23.940 --> 01:12:25.610
I'm trying to think about
like how it went down.

01:12:25.610 --> 01:12:29.433
Nonetheless, VaynerSports
is only football right now.

01:12:30.550 --> 01:12:32.480
The next two sports that we'll expand into

01:12:32.480 --> 01:12:34.720
based on mine and A.J.'s interests

01:12:34.720 --> 01:12:38.080
are most likely esports and the NBA.

01:12:38.080 --> 01:12:40.320
We haven't really thought about going into

01:12:40.320 --> 01:12:43.670
repping talent in the UFC
and mixed martial arts.

01:12:43.670 --> 01:12:45.730
I'm extremely bullish on it.

01:12:45.730 --> 01:12:49.513
I think it's an extremely
lucrative category and territory.

01:12:51.190 --> 01:12:54.630
And so, we haven't thought
about expanding it there next

01:12:54.630 --> 01:12:56.830
'cause we've got a
little bit of a road map.

01:12:59.170 --> 01:13:01.180
A.J.'s really running VaynerSports

01:13:01.180 --> 01:13:03.320
and I'm like creating the halo effect.

01:13:03.320 --> 01:13:05.420
And so I'll have to react to where

01:13:05.420 --> 01:13:07.520
he sees some of the opportunities as well.

01:13:08.410 --> 01:13:09.243
So that's kind of where we're at.

01:13:09.243 --> 01:13:10.400
But like, A--

01:13:10.400 --> 01:13:11.233
Yeah, please

01:13:11.233 --> 01:13:13.800
- The athletes make a fraction in MMA

01:13:13.800 --> 01:13:15.520
of what's sort of repping them.

01:13:15.520 --> 01:13:17.230
There's not as much money
to be made in MMA athlete

01:13:17.230 --> 01:13:20.680
compared to NBA or NFL or anything else.

01:13:20.680 --> 01:13:22.980
- Yeah, I mean I think
that can change, right?

01:13:24.013 --> 01:13:27.050
Yeah I never make decisions
based on what it is now,

01:13:27.050 --> 01:13:29.270
it's more about my
anticipation to your point.

01:13:29.270 --> 01:13:32.007
It'll be interesting
to see how it evolves.

01:13:32.007 --> 01:13:35.470
Look, I think fighting,
you know, in whatever form

01:13:35.470 --> 01:13:39.150
is always quite lucrative
'cause it's so primal to us.

01:13:39.150 --> 01:13:40.750
The thought of like the big event

01:13:40.750 --> 01:13:44.650
where two people fight is so

01:13:44.650 --> 01:13:47.300
100% always gonna be there.

01:13:47.300 --> 01:13:50.290
For us, we just have a lot
of interest in the NBA,

01:13:50.290 --> 01:13:52.960
and the esports thing is
super interesting to me.

01:13:52.960 --> 01:13:56.820
Like to me, if VaynerSports
was here 12 years ago

01:13:56.820 --> 01:13:58.170
I would've done UFC.

01:13:58.170 --> 01:14:01.920
To me I wanna catch something
in a different part,

01:14:01.920 --> 01:14:04.200
you know NBA and NFL's interest graph

01:14:05.214 --> 01:14:08.610
esports over UFC on the base
of the maturity of the market.

01:14:08.610 --> 01:14:09.930
The less mature something is,

01:14:09.930 --> 01:14:11.480
the more opportunity there is.

01:14:11.480 --> 01:14:14.163
And so for me, I wanna be looking at that.

01:14:15.012 --> 01:14:15.845
- [Man In Gray Shirt] Thank you.

01:14:15.845 --> 01:14:17.137
- You're welcome.

01:14:17.137 --> 01:14:19.077
(audience applauding)

01:14:19.077 --> 01:14:20.457
- Okay, one last question and then--

01:14:20.457 --> 01:14:22.520
- Yeah, that's good.

01:14:22.520 --> 01:14:23.353
- Hi.

01:14:23.353 --> 01:14:24.770
- Hi, Luisa.

01:14:24.770 --> 01:14:27.237
So my question may not
apply to many of you

01:14:27.237 --> 01:14:28.560
but it was triggered by

01:14:28.560 --> 01:14:31.077
what you said about being an immigrant.

01:14:31.077 --> 01:14:31.910
- [Gary] Yes.

01:14:31.910 --> 01:14:32.743
- 'Cause I'm one of them.

01:14:32.743 --> 01:14:33.576
- [Gary] Yes, I can tell.

01:14:33.576 --> 01:14:34.409
- From Poland.

01:14:34.409 --> 01:14:35.242
- [Gary] Yes.

01:14:35.242 --> 01:14:36.744
- So what would you advise

01:14:36.744 --> 01:14:38.753
to the person who came from
the Communistic country

01:14:38.753 --> 01:14:42.403
who came with the mindset
of working super hard,

01:14:43.300 --> 01:14:44.400
I know you're laughing already

01:14:44.400 --> 01:14:45.483
because I spoke with you about it.

01:14:45.483 --> 01:14:48.170
So working super hard and you finally

01:14:48.170 --> 01:14:50.960
end up being just trapped
that even when you succeed

01:14:50.960 --> 01:14:53.540
at like, you know, thanks to the people at

01:14:53.540 --> 01:14:57.430
my school, I grew by 400% over two years.

01:14:57.430 --> 01:14:59.020
So that's quite a big hit.

01:14:59.020 --> 01:14:59.853
- [Gary] Yes.

01:14:59.853 --> 01:15:01.906
So now everything goes so much better,

01:15:01.906 --> 01:15:06.008
I end up not being able to
stop myself from working.

01:15:06.008 --> 01:15:06.841
- [Gary] Do you want to?

01:15:06.841 --> 01:15:09.720
- And there's a fear
of just failing down--

01:15:09.720 --> 01:15:10.553
- [Gary] Sure.

01:15:10.553 --> 01:15:12.664
- 'Cause what if I lose
everything what I have?

01:15:12.664 --> 01:15:13.497
- [Gary] Yup.

01:15:13.497 --> 01:15:15.680
- I also feel like I'm in a
conflict of the whole family,

01:15:15.680 --> 01:15:18.900
and mindset of my whole family

01:15:18.900 --> 01:15:20.097
because now I think different

01:15:20.097 --> 01:15:23.750
and I know I can be happy,
I know I can be grateful

01:15:23.750 --> 01:15:25.180
and I know I can succeed

01:15:25.180 --> 01:15:27.700
but Polish people don't think this way

01:15:27.700 --> 01:15:30.772
because we're used to just
being communistic country

01:15:30.772 --> 01:15:31.890
and always not having anything.

01:15:31.890 --> 01:15:33.460
- [Gary] I'm aware.

01:15:33.460 --> 01:15:35.360
So, I mean, look there's a lot there.

01:15:35.360 --> 01:15:37.270
And stay here so we can go back and forth.

01:15:37.270 --> 01:15:38.110
Stay at the mic.

01:15:38.110 --> 01:15:40.170
So I think look, first of all

01:15:40.170 --> 01:15:42.410
the back half of your question

01:15:42.410 --> 01:15:44.880
was the whole point that
I made earlier which is

01:15:46.567 --> 01:15:48.950
if you could go inside my brain

01:15:48.950 --> 01:15:51.060
and my feelings and my DNA right now,

01:15:51.060 --> 01:15:54.010
it would either scare you or confuse you

01:15:54.010 --> 01:15:59.010
how much I do not allow my
wife, children or parents

01:15:59.350 --> 01:16:01.840
to factor into the way
I think about things.

01:16:01.840 --> 01:16:04.963
At the same token, their
opinions of me are my life.

01:16:05.860 --> 01:16:08.810
You have to find the
calibration of respecting

01:16:10.130 --> 01:16:11.450
people's opinions,

01:16:11.450 --> 01:16:15.160
but now allowing them
to dictate your actions

01:16:15.160 --> 01:16:17.740
because you're gonna go down the path

01:16:17.740 --> 01:16:20.030
of becoming bitter with them at the end.

01:16:20.030 --> 01:16:23.050
Too many of us protect our
family and pander to them

01:16:23.050 --> 01:16:24.530
because we wanted to be good,

01:16:24.530 --> 01:16:27.050
without realizing how
it plays out in the end

01:16:27.050 --> 01:16:28.720
which is in our older years.

01:16:28.720 --> 01:16:31.100
We have a lot of resentment towards them

01:16:31.100 --> 01:16:34.420
'cause we think we allowed
them to dictate our behavior.

01:16:34.420 --> 01:16:36.680
But that's not true.

01:16:36.680 --> 01:16:39.960
So you know, listen, we
share a lot common themes.

01:16:39.960 --> 01:16:41.580
I understand.

01:16:41.580 --> 01:16:44.660
First of all, on the working part,

01:16:44.660 --> 01:16:46.200
first you have to ask yourself if you,

01:16:46.200 --> 01:16:48.230
do you want to work less?

01:16:48.230 --> 01:16:49.070
I'm asking.

01:16:49.070 --> 01:16:49.903
- [Luisa] Yes.

01:16:49.903 --> 01:16:51.113
- Well then work less.

01:16:51.113 --> 01:16:52.404
(audience laughing)

01:16:52.404 --> 01:16:53.280
- [Luisa] Yes.

01:16:53.280 --> 01:16:54.424
- You know what I mean?

01:16:54.424 --> 01:16:56.550
The way you gotta think about it is,

01:16:56.550 --> 01:16:58.010
whatever management you put in or

01:16:58.010 --> 01:16:59.890
whatever happens, first you have to

01:16:59.890 --> 01:17:01.943
immediately think it's gonna do less.

01:17:03.450 --> 01:17:07.080
Second, you can't hold
your managers accountable.

01:17:07.080 --> 01:17:10.630
One thing I know about
eastern European employers

01:17:10.630 --> 01:17:12.460
is when they do moves like that

01:17:12.460 --> 01:17:13.900
they expect those people to work

01:17:13.900 --> 01:17:15.740
like a horse the way they did.

01:17:15.740 --> 01:17:17.220
It's not their business.

01:17:17.220 --> 01:17:18.630
Unless you're willing to give your manager

01:17:18.630 --> 01:17:19.950
the same amount of money

01:17:19.950 --> 01:17:21.120
and a piece of the business,

01:17:21.120 --> 01:17:23.830
why should he or she work as hard as you?

01:17:23.830 --> 01:17:27.420
So first you have to deploy
practicality, reality.

01:17:27.420 --> 01:17:30.640
And everything, my friends, has a price.

01:17:30.640 --> 01:17:32.170
Everything.

01:17:32.170 --> 01:17:34.260
So if you want to work less,

01:17:34.260 --> 01:17:37.200
and take spa treatment and go fishing

01:17:37.200 --> 01:17:39.690
and pick up basketball
or learn how to sing,

01:17:39.690 --> 01:17:41.630
or whatever the fuck you want,

01:17:41.630 --> 01:17:43.020
well know that it comes at the expense

01:17:43.020 --> 01:17:44.640
of your business growing.

01:17:44.640 --> 01:17:45.623
And that's okay.

01:17:46.850 --> 01:17:48.770
And once you learn how to stop

01:17:48.770 --> 01:17:51.430
thinking about the judgment
of others on your behavior,

01:17:51.430 --> 01:17:53.340
everything opens up.

01:17:53.340 --> 01:17:56.280
Easy to say but it
takes a lot of practice.

01:17:56.280 --> 01:17:57.190
And it starts with,

01:17:57.190 --> 01:18:00.320
the reason I always say
fuck you mom, fuck you dad.

01:18:00.320 --> 01:18:02.230
It starts with practice.

01:18:02.230 --> 01:18:03.510
If you sit down in your family and be like

01:18:03.510 --> 01:18:04.600
I'm doing this,

01:18:04.600 --> 01:18:07.140
I know exactly what you're thinking.

01:18:07.140 --> 01:18:08.190
It's my life.

01:18:08.190 --> 01:18:09.840
I'm sorry if it hurts your feelings

01:18:09.840 --> 01:18:10.710
this is what I'm doing.

01:18:10.710 --> 01:18:11.900
'Cause I don't wanna resent.

01:18:11.900 --> 01:18:13.550
The way I do it is tell the truth,

01:18:13.550 --> 01:18:15.263
I don't want to resent you later.

01:18:17.120 --> 01:18:18.860
I always tell people, whenever
I had to have that talk

01:18:18.860 --> 01:18:20.790
with my dad or mom or brother,

01:18:20.790 --> 01:18:23.510
I always tell people, I'm gonna break.

01:18:23.510 --> 01:18:25.803
And if I break, then it's all broken.

01:18:28.160 --> 01:18:30.270
And I promise you, when
you put them into a corner

01:18:30.270 --> 01:18:32.250
instead of them putting you into a corner,

01:18:32.250 --> 01:18:33.130
it gets real funny.

01:18:33.130 --> 01:18:37.100
I'm fascinated by bullying in general

01:18:37.100 --> 01:18:39.853
and families bully the
moneymaker in their family.

01:18:41.520 --> 01:18:42.530
And a funny thing happens

01:18:42.530 --> 01:18:44.870
when you go and treat them like a bully.

01:18:44.870 --> 01:18:46.470
They fold like a cheap chair,

01:18:46.470 --> 01:18:48.320
'cause they have no fucking leverage.

01:18:50.231 --> 01:18:51.600
(Gary laughing)

01:18:51.600 --> 01:18:52.850
You like that right?

01:18:52.850 --> 01:18:54.130
Hits home right?

01:18:54.130 --> 01:18:57.683
When you're the moneymaker,
everybody gets real used to you.

01:18:58.770 --> 01:19:01.563
When you flip it on them,
they've got no move.

01:19:02.490 --> 01:19:03.640
Let them go make money.

01:19:05.464 --> 01:19:06.297
- [Luisa] Thank you.

01:19:06.297 --> 01:19:07.130
- You're welcome.

01:19:07.130 --> 01:19:10.297
(audience applauding)

01:19:11.958 --> 01:19:14.510
It's a real thing, like
it's hard for a lot of us.

01:19:14.510 --> 01:19:17.130
If we're the driver,
people get into a cadence

01:19:18.174 --> 01:19:19.680
and look when you know how to make money

01:19:19.680 --> 01:19:21.630
you start taking on almost
this responsibility.

01:19:21.630 --> 01:19:22.463
You start helping.

01:19:22.463 --> 01:19:23.296
You love your family,

01:19:23.296 --> 01:19:24.129
I love everybody.

01:19:24.129 --> 01:19:25.793
I fucking love you guys, I
don't even fucking know you.

01:19:25.793 --> 01:19:26.751
- [Man In Audience] Thank you.

01:19:26.751 --> 01:19:27.584
- You know?

01:19:27.584 --> 01:19:29.630
Like you start getting into that place

01:19:29.630 --> 01:19:31.830
and then everybody gets
into their position.

01:19:32.930 --> 01:19:34.550
I'm okay with it, you're okay with it,

01:19:34.550 --> 01:19:35.383
we'll get to you in a second.

01:19:35.383 --> 01:19:37.400
Like you can be okay with it

01:19:37.400 --> 01:19:39.200
you can be okay with eating
shit your whole life.

01:19:39.200 --> 01:19:42.640
I've eaten more shit than
anybody i've ever seen.

01:19:42.640 --> 01:19:43.763
The problem is.

01:19:44.668 --> 01:19:46.420
No, no problem.

01:19:46.420 --> 01:19:49.060
The problem is, once you're at a place

01:19:49.060 --> 01:19:51.410
where you don't want to
do it anymore, you act.

01:19:53.090 --> 01:19:54.630
See what their move is to that.

01:19:54.630 --> 01:19:57.520
It's just practice, one time.

01:19:57.520 --> 01:19:58.740
Not when you're drunk.

01:19:58.740 --> 01:20:02.330
Not when it's so crazy that
you can't deal with it anymore.

01:20:02.330 --> 01:20:04.990
A month, a year before you break

01:20:04.990 --> 01:20:07.320
and go crazy and yell at them
at the top of your lungs.

01:20:07.320 --> 01:20:10.090
Calm nice dinner and be
like here's the score.

01:20:10.090 --> 01:20:10.923
It's incredible.

01:20:10.923 --> 01:20:11.930
I've given this advice a lot,

01:20:11.930 --> 01:20:14.900
it's been game changing
for people's lives.

01:20:14.900 --> 01:20:16.230
When they've acted on it

01:20:16.230 --> 01:20:18.933
most don't act on it, 'cause it's hard.

01:20:20.060 --> 01:20:22.280
I don't think what I just said is easy.

01:20:22.280 --> 01:20:24.540
It's super hard.

01:20:24.540 --> 01:20:27.483
And the longer it's been
real, the harder it is, right?

01:20:28.508 --> 01:20:29.818
- [Kelly] Hi there, I'm Kelly.

01:20:29.818 --> 01:20:30.651
- Hi Kelly.

01:20:30.651 --> 01:20:33.071
- [Kelly] I work for Michael.
- Very nice, sorry.

01:20:33.071 --> 01:20:36.710
(audience laughs)

01:20:36.710 --> 01:20:38.180
- So as you mentioned before,

01:20:38.180 --> 01:20:40.620
this is a media business first.

01:20:40.620 --> 01:20:42.492
And obviously I look at Proxain.

01:20:42.492 --> 01:20:44.190
we have over 250 locations open.

01:20:44.190 --> 01:20:46.280
Another 800 to open soon.

01:20:46.280 --> 01:20:47.430
- [Gary] Incredible.

01:20:47.430 --> 01:20:48.550
- It does become difficult when

01:20:48.550 --> 01:20:50.030
you have lots of different levels of

01:20:50.030 --> 01:20:52.640
competency when it comes
to our franchisees.

01:20:52.640 --> 01:20:54.330
Some of them don't even
have a Facebook to start.

01:20:54.330 --> 01:20:55.300
- [Gary] Yes.

01:20:55.300 --> 01:20:57.740
